|-|Trivia=
[[File:800px-HeatColt654-1.jpg|thumb|320px|The mask worn by McCauley in Heat. This was likely the inspiration for the Hockey Heat mask. Unsurprising, seeing how Overkill Software seems to enjoy paying homages to this film.]]
*The '''Mark''' mask was added in ''PAYDAY 2'' as a reference to [[w:c:hotlinemiami:Mark|Mark]] from ''{{w|Hotline Miami 2: Wrong Number}}'', which the developers of the game were able to play a very early build of.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/paydaytheheist/comments/4d60gn/last_5_mega_masks/d1oa964</ref>
**The Overkill bomb logo can be found in the eyes of the mask.
*The '''Hockey Heat''' masks were worn by the main character's crew, most notably the heister McCauley, in the 1995 film ''{{w|Heat (1995 film)|Heat}}''. The same character wearing the same mask in the screenshot on the right is likely the inspiration of the [[Armored Transport (DLC)|Armored Transport]] DLC splash card as well.
*The '''Peter''' mask is based on the [[w:c:hotlinemiami:Peter Mask|''Hotline Miami'' mask of the same name]].
*'''The Terminator''' glasses are a reference to the {{w|The Terminator|1984 film of the same name}}. They are based on the glasses worn by the eponymous antagonist throughout the film, with the description referencing the Terminator's origin ("an assassin from a distant land", "built like a machine").
*The '''Reservoir Dog''' glasses are named after the 1992 film ''{{w|Reservoir Dogs}}''. The glasses resemble those worn by the main characters, who had indeed all worn the same clothing and had codenames.
*The '''Conquest''', '''Death''', '''Famine''', and '''War''' masks are all rather obviously based on the {{w|Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse}}.
</tabber>

