|-|Trivia=
*The '''Alienware''' mask is a promotion from a computer hardware company called {{w|Alienware}}, {{w|Dell Technologies|Dell}}'s subsidiary; the mask is the company's mascot, the Alien. It must be found like the rest of the masks in ''[[PAYDAY 2]]'', unlike in ''[[PAYDAY: The Heist]]'' where it's given exclusively to anyone with an Alienware computer.
*The '''Brainiac''' mask is an homage to {{w|Jason Voorhees}}' look in ''{{w|Jason Goes to Hell: The Final Friday}}''.
*The '''Calaca''' mask is from the Mexican Spanish word {{w|Calaca}}, which is a skull or skeleton commonly used for the {{w|Day of the Dead|Mexican Day of the Dead}}.
*The '''Doctor Crime''' mask is a homage to {{w|Doctor Doom}} by {{w|Marvel Comics}}.
*The '''Greek Tragedy''' mask is derived from the masks found in {{w|Greek tragedy|Greek tragedies}}, a form of theater from Ancient Greece and Asia Minor.
*The '''Hockey Mask''' was worn by the character "Waingro" in the 1995 film, ''{{w|Heat (1995 film)|Heat}}''.
*The '''Hog''' mask is a homage to ''{{w|Hotline Miami}}'', a game developed by {{w|Dennaton Games}}.
*The '''Jaw''' mask is likely a reference to [[w:c:he-man:Trap Jaw|Trap Jaw]] from the ''{{w|He-Man and the Masters of the Universe}}'' series.
*'''Kenneth''' is credited as "Janitor" in the Payday 2 credits.
*'''Mr. Smooth''' is based on singer {{w|David Bowie}}, bearing a strong resemblance to the his Ziggy Stardust persona. The masks' description of merging beings is likely an homage to Bowie's many different characters and personas.
*The '''Mummy''' mask is based on {{w|Iron Maiden}}'s mascot {{w|Eddie the Head|Eddie}} from the {{w|Powerslave}} album.
*The '''Oni''' mask is from {{w|Japanese folklore}}, {{w|Oni}} meaning "demon".
*The '''Outlander''' mask is a reference to {{w|I Have No Mouth, and I Must Scream}}, a short story by {{w|Harlan Ellison}}, published in March, 1967. It later turned into a {{w|I Have No Mouth, and I Must Scream (video game)|point-and-click adventure game}} in 1995 by {{w|The Dreamers Guild}}. The story was based in a post-apocalyptic future set 109 years into the future after the Cold War escalated into a World War controlled by a Super Computer named AM in which it nearly wiped out the human race in a massive genocide. The mask represents the ending of the protagonist turning into a [http://lparchive.org/I-Have-No-Mouth-and-I-Must-Scream/Update%2071/images/s_033.png gelatinous blob creature] wanting to scream of the horrors it suffered but cannot due to its lack of a mouth, forever condemned to its thoughts.
*The '''{{w|Shrunken head|Shrunken Head}}''' mask is from a practice that includes severing and shrinking a human head that is used for rituals, trophies, or for trade.
*The '''Vampire''' mask is based on the iconic vampire {{w|Count Dracula}}.
