|-|Trivia=
*The '''Strinch''' mask and its associated achievement ("Stealing Christmas") are references to the Dr. Seuss book ''{{w|How the Grinch Stole Christmas!}}''.
**The piece that is supposed to resemble a nose is has a fleur-de-lis on it, a symbol associated with the [[PAYDAY Secret ARG]].
*The '''Krampus''' mask and its description are references to the mythical Germanic {{w|Krampus|entity of the same name}}.
*The '''Mechanical Santa''' mask is based on the murderous [http://theinfosphere.org/Robot_Santa_Claus Robot Santa Claus] from ''{{w|Futurama}}''.
*The '''Mrs. Claus''', '''Strinch''', '''Mechanical Santa''', and '''Krampus''' masks were designed by [http://www.overkillsoftware.com/whitechristmas/ community members] that [http://youtu.be/da1u9GyE_oM defeated Almir in the "bull challenge"] in Los Angeles.
*The '''Tids''' is a reference to {{w|The Stig}}, a recurring character in the British TV show ''{{w|Top Gear (2002 TV series)|Top Gear}}''. The helmet is based on a Simpson Diamondback helmet which The Stig wears.
*Three of the four masks introduced on the final day of the [[PAYDAY 2 Community Events#CrimeFest 2015|2015 CrimeFest]] are based on internet memes: While the '''Dawg''' and '''No Me Gusta''' masks are based on the [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/doge Doge] (and name probably a reference to [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/xzibit-yo-dawg Yo Dawg]) and [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/me-gusta Me Gusta] memes respectively, the '''Rageface''' mask is a mix of the [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/lol-guy LOL], [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/rage-guy-fffffuuuuuuuu Rage], and [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/y-u-no-guy Y U NO] memes.
**The '''Funnyman''' mask was originally named '''Baitface''', and its [[:Image:2015-10-24 00019.jpg|original appearance and description]] was based on the [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/trollface-coolface-problem Trollface] meme, but the mask's appearance was changed to what it currently is in [[PC update history (Payday 2) Old#Update #90|Update #90]], and its name and description were changed later on. No official reason has been given but it's likely because the creator of the Trollface put a copyright on the image.
***The Funnyman mask is from an unused version of [[Dallas]]' [[Masks#Troll|Troll mask]] from ''[[PAYDAY: The Heist]]''.
*The '''Rudelf''' mask is a reference to {{w|Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer}}, and the mask's name is a pun on "Rudolph" and "Elf", and could be interpreted as a pun on "Rude" and "Elf" as well.
