[[File:Batch 1 Overkill masks.jpg|300px|thumb|right|Concept art for the first five post-release COMPLETELY OVERKILL masks.]][[File:COP-Masks.jpg|300px|thumb|right|Concept art for the final five post-release COMPLETELY OVERKILL masks. Note the mask in the lower-right corner.]]
*The masks introduced in updates [[PC update history (Payday 2) Old#Update #95.3|#95.3]] and [[PC update history (Payday 2)#Update #103|#103]] were released due to the backlash in response to the COMPLETELY OVERKILL Pack's "secret content" being [[Safes (Gameplay)|weapon skins]]. They were based on the most commonly worn masks by players.
*The '''Mega Kawaii''' mask is a reference to the ''[[wikipedia:Sailor Moon|Sailor Moon]]'' franchise.
*The '''Mega Kevin''' mask is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Predator (film)|first]] [[wikipedia:Predator 2|two]] films of the ''Predator'' franchise and the actor who played the titular extraterrestrial in those movies, [[wikipedia:Kevin Peter Hall|Kevin Peter Hall]].
*The legendary bear mentioned in the '''Mega Mark''''s description may refer to the [[wikipedia:Nandi Bear|Nandi Bear]]. Alternatively, it may be a reference to [[w:c:disney:Mor'du|Mor'du]] from the 2012 film ''[[wikipedia:Brave (2012 film)|Brave]]''.
*The '''Mega Watcher''' mask was originally supposed to be a '''Mega Zombie''' mask, but was changed for reasons unknown.<!-- can someone find out if there was an actual reason for this --> The following was to be the Mega Zombie's description, from the [http://steamcommunity.com/games/218620/announcements/detail/854930376620930003 announcement of the final five COMPLETELY OVERKILL Pack masks]: "All his life Jeremy only wanted was to be a dentist, but fate had other plans for him. After dying in a gruesome car-crash, he was somehow animated back to life again. Unfortunately, his past dreams died the day of the crash, and the only thing Jeremy wants now is to suck out the brains of the living."
</tabber>

