Maui.png|{{Mask tooltip|Maui|color=dlc|2015-12-04 00011.jpg|Exploring the Pacific "Ring of Fire" in his youth, Bodhi came to the following revelation: honoring oneself means honoring the myths. A myth that stuck with him was that of Maui. Like Bodhi, Maui was a dauntless champion of humankind, a trickster and adventurer.|{{color|dlc|'''THIS IS A POINT BREAK HEISTS ITEM!'''}}}}<br>Unlocked through<br>Achievement
Oro.png|{{Mask tooltip|Oro|color=dlc|2015-12-04 00012.jpg|It was exploring the Islands of French Polynesia, Bodhi encountered the disciples of the war-god Oro. The young adventurer quickly became enamored of this god, who valued the appreciation of beautiful crafts as much as the art of struggle.|{{color|dlc|'''THIS IS A POINT BREAK HEISTS ITEM!'''}}}}<br>Unlocked through<br>Achievement
Tane.png|{{Mask tooltip|Tane|color=dlc|2015-12-04 00013.jpg|Tane was the god of the forest who used his mighty strength to separate his parents, the earth and the sky. Legends also credit him with creating Tiki, the first man. Thus, he created the world as we know it, and the people within it.|{{color|dlc|'''THIS IS A POINT BREAK HEISTS ITEM!'''}}}}<br>Unlocked through<br>Achievement
Tawhiri.png|{{Mask tooltip|Tawhiri|color=dlc|2015-12-04 00014.jpg|Brother of Tane, Tawhiri is the god of weather, most particularly violent storms and lightning. Bodhi experienced plenty of both, and it was during a particularly vicious explosion while reef-diving in Tuvalu that Bodhi gained a true appreciation for this powerful deity.|{{color|dlc|'''THIS IS A POINT BREAK HEISTS ITEM!'''}}}}<br>Unlocked through<br>Achievement
</gallery>
|-|Trivia=
*The masks from the Point Break Heists DLC are all based on figures from [[wikipedia:Maori mythology|Maori mythology]], save for the '''Oro''' mask.
**'''[[wikipedia:Maui (Maori mythology)|Maui]]''' is a culture hero in Maori mythology, indeed known for his trickery.
***The design of the Maui mask appears to be based on the face of [[wikipedia:The Joker (The Dark Knight)|The Joker]] from ''[[wikipedia:The Dark Knight (film)|The Dark Knight]]'' film, most notably possessing his [[wikipedia:Glasgow smile|Glasgow smile clown makeup]].
**Unlike the other three masks from this set, '''[[wikipedia:'Oro|'Oro]]''' is not a part of Maori mythology, he is rather a god from [[wikipedia:Polynesian narrative|Polynesian mythology]], which the rituals, beliefs, and world view the Maori mythology had inherited from. 'Oro was known as the god of war, who would in times of peace turn into the god of the fine arts.
**'''[[wikipedia:Tane|Tane]]''' is the god of the forest, who had indeed separated his parents, the gods of the earth and the sky, [[wikipedia:Rangi and Papa|Ranginui and Papatuanuku]], and some legends do say he created the first of humankind, [[wikipedia:Tiki|Tiki]].
**[[wikipedia:Tawhirimatea|Tawhirimatea]], also known as '''Tawhiri''', is the god of weather, a son of Ranginui and Papatuanuku, and brother of Tane.
</tabber>

