|-|Trivia=
* The '''Frank''' mask is a reference to the character [[wikipedia:Frankenstein's monster|Frankenstein's monster]].
* The '''Venomorph''' mask is a homage to ''[[wikipedia:Alien (film)|Alien]]'', a 1979 sci-fi horror film by [[wikipedia:Ridley Scott|Ridley Scott]]. The name of the achievement regarding the mask is also a part of the movie's theatrical title ("In space, no one can hear you scream!"). It could also be a reference to the character [[Wikipedia:Venom (comics)|Venom]] from ''[[Wikipedia:The Amazing Spider-Man|The Amazing Spider-Man]]'' franchise, as seen [http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=241276457 here].
* The '''Cry Baby''' is based on a picture taken by Andreas Häll Penninger from his son. Andreas is a producer at OVERKILL. ''[https://twitter.com/paydad_/status/1314202373783420928?s=21 Twitter]''
* The '''Brazil Baby''' mask is a reference to the 1985 dystopian satire sci-fi, ''[[wikipedia:Brazil (1985 film)|Brazil]]'', based on a mask worn by the character "[http://movieimages.tripod.com/brazil/brazil29.jpg Jack Lint]" in an interrogation room. Coincidentally, [[wikipedia:Robert De Niro|Robert De Niro]] plays a character in both ''[[wikipedia:Heat (1995 film)|Heat]]'' and Brazil.
* The '''Invader''' mask is based on the aliens from the movies ''[[wikipedia:Mars Attacks!|Mars Attacks!]]'' and ''[[wikipedia:They Live|They Live]]''.
